## Analytical Significance for PRIS Research

### For P3 (BFSI AI Governance Regulatory Parallelism, JEIM) and fsQCA
DPDP Rules 2025 is the foundational data-governance layer that the RBI FREE-AI Committee Report explicitly cross-references as the applicable framework for AI "Data Lifecycle Governance" obligations in regulated entities. This creates a direct **parallelism/coordination test case**: RBI (sectoral prudential regulator) issuing AI-specific governance expectations that incorporate, by reference, a horizontal data-protection instrument issued by MeitY (a different regulator, different statutory basis). This is strong evidence for the Regulatory Parallelism construct — two regulators governing overlapping data-handling obligations for AI systems without a single integrated instrument.

### Coordination / Parallelism Pattern
Existing node: [[07_Institutions/Corpus/RBI/RBI_FREE_AI_2025]] (this batch). Pattern: **Unidirectional incorporation-by-reference** — RBI's AI governance framework defers to DPDP for data lifecycle compliance but does not itself create enforcement linkage to the Data Protection Board. This is a candidate "governance debt" indicator: regulated entities must satisfy both RBI supervisory expectations and DPDB compliance obligations, assessed independently.

